tuigreet in the style of the Plymouth theme "arch-mono": black screen, the classic Arch
logo (fastfetch "arch") in Arch blue, username/password with • dots under it, dim clock.

gen.py OUT [classic|outline|blocks] writes:
  OUT/config.toml  -> /etc/tuigreet/config.toml   (greetd runs tuigreet --config it)
  OUT/vtrgb        -> /etc/tuigreet/vtrgb         (VT palette: logo = #d0d0d0 ...)
The palette is applied before greetd starts by
  /etc/systemd/system/greetd.service.d/vt-palette.conf  (ExecStartPre=-/usr/bin/setvtrgb ...)

Preview without logging out: tuigreet --mock --config /etc/tuigreet/config.toml
(in a terminal emulator the colours are the terminal's, not the VT palette).
The console font is ter-v24b (no ▀▄ half blocks, no katakana) — only use glyphs it has.
Never restart greetd from inside a session, it ends the session.
